---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import NewTabLink from "../components/NewTabLink.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="About"
    description="Why this tool exists, what to do with it, how to contribute, and acknowledgements."
>
    <header class="header header--plain">
        <h1 class="header__title">About</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="content">
        <figure class="quote">
            <blockquote>
                <p>
                    Any person may be able-bodied for the moment. But everyone
                    will at some point suffer from at least one or more chronic
                    diseases and be disabled.
                </p>
            </blockquote>
            <figcaption>
                Irving Zola, quoted in{" "}
                <NewTabLink href="https://web.archive.org/web/2005/http://www.ragged-edge-mag.com/0999/b0999ft2.html">
                    <cite>The Ragged Edge</cite>
                </NewTabLink>
                , 1999
            </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p>
            Irving Zola (1935-1994) was a sociologist and disability rights
            activist who had polio as a teenager. He argued that disability
            isn't the concern of a small minority, but something nearly all of
            us will live with at some point, and that we should design and make
            policy with that in mind. When it's our turn we'll want the web to
            work, so let's do better.
        </p>

        <h2 class="eyebrow--highlight">What to do with it</h2>
        <p>
            It's not an exhaustive list of human needs, or a collection of
            personas. Have a click through to read, come back when you're stuck
            or think you're finished and want to test your product through the
            experience of others. Maybe try using it in your next design crit.
            Each scenario has a unique URL, so share if you think it would help
            someone.
        </p>

        <h2 class="eyebrow--highlight">How to contribute</h2>
        <p>
            We're open to contributions! Head to our{" "}
            <NewTabLink href="https://github.com/jackbush/zola">
                GitHub
            </NewTabLink>{" "}
            to get involved.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Contribute a scenario</li>
            <li>Give feedback</li>
            <li>Report or fix a bug</li>
            <li>Improve the look</li>
            <li>Share an idea</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="eyebrow--highlight">Acknowledgements</h2>
        <p>
            Initial scenarios adapted from{" "}
            <NewTabLink href="https://web.archive.org/web/20160319032044/https://the-pastry-box-project.net/anne-gibson/2014-july-31">
                <cite>An Alphabet of Accessibility Issues</cite> by Anne Gibson
            </NewTabLink>
            .
        </p>
    </div>
</Layout>

<style>
    .quote {
        margin: 0 0 40px;

        & blockquote {
            margin: 0 0 16px;
        }

        & blockquote p {
            font-size: clamp(1.625rem, 4.5vw, 2.375rem);
            font-weight: 700;
            line-height: 1.2;
            letter-spacing: -0.01em;
            margin: 0;
        }

        & figcaption {
            color: var(--muted);
            font-size: clamp(0.875rem, 1.8vw, 1rem);
        }
    }
</style>
